IanMaclure (maclure@eos.arc.nasa.gov) wrote:
: On a multi-processor AXP ( 2100? ) ( under OpenVMS and OSF1 ) is 
: it possible to specify that a given process be loaded into a 
: predetermined CPU and remain there for the life of the process. 
: I am definitely not interested in SMP as the processes are NOT
: in general symmetric.

: IBM

On OSF/1, try man 4 processor_sets
or even better try man 3 bind_to_cpu

  Upon return from bind_to_cpu, all threads of the target pid are running on
  the target CPU.  Bound threads are not eligible for execution on any other
  CPU. You release CPU binding by invoking bind_to_cpu with a  cpu_mask of
  zero.

I am not sure if this was available in V3.0 of OSF/1 but it is there in
the latest release of it.

