X-Deja-AN: 101595446
organization: Malaspina University-College
newsgroups: comp.os.vms,comp.sys.dec,vmsnet.misc


We are having a rather strange problem with a Datatrieve procedure.

At the point where the procedure is attempting to do a "DEFINE FILE"
to create a data file for a temporary domain we get the following error:

%CDD-F-NOWRITE, no privilege to write SYS$SYSDEVICE:[CDDPLUS]
Reinitializing CDD 

This strikes me as particularly odd since the "DEFINE FILE" command only
creates a data file, it doesn't make any changes to the CDD. The procedure
is able to define domains and records in this dictionary without any
problems, it's only when it attempts to create a data file that this
error seems to occur. It also seems the error is not 100% reproducible,
at several points of fiddling with protection codes I managed to get
the command to work, but subsequent attempts would fail again. By
extracting the entire dictionary and reloading it into a different path
I managed to get the problem to go away, but I'm not confident that it
won't come back later ( as per my previous temporary successes )

The relevant versions are:

  Datatrieve 6.0
  CDD 5.1
  Rdb 4.0-2

 (yes, I know the Rdb version is ancient, but we have some software
linked to this version and the supplier refuses to send us a version
linked with a more recent version)

  I tend to suspect this is a Datatrieve problem, since it appears to
have no reason to attempt to do any writing to the CDD at the failure
point.

  Any pointers would be appreciated.

