Message-ID: <3nlmft$mgn@spool.cs.wisc.edu>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 101595431
organization: University of WI, Madison -- Computer Sciences Dept.
newsgroups: comp.sys.dec


In order to make it easier for atmosphere and ocean modelers to
distribute their data sets, we have defined Vis5D files as a medium
for exchanging information on the World Wide Web.  Vis5D is a
freeware system specifically designed for interactively visualizing
environmental simulations.  Links to Vis5D files can be embedded in
Web pages (just as links to GIF files can be embedded in Web pages),
and Mosaic can automatically invoke Vis5D to view them (just as it
automatically invokes xv to view GIF files).

The information about how to do this is on the Web page at URL:

  http://www.ssec.wisc.edu/~billh/view5d.html

Of course, Vis5D files can be pretty large so transfers may be too
slow to be useful in some cases.  Nevertheless, we think that there
are many cases where using Vis5D files as a Web medium can be useful.

Please let us know at whibbard@macc.wisc@edu (Bill Hibbard) or
brianp@ssec.wisc.edu (Brian Paul) if you have any questions or
problems.




