It depends on the generation, of course. The SPECfp of the clock-doubled 
66mhz 601 sans L2 cache was only 33% higher than the 66mhz P5 on a 66mhz 
data bus with 512K of L2 cache, but the clock-tripled 100mhz 604 sans L2 
cache gets about 145 SPECfp92 compared to the 1.5:1 90mhz P54c WITH L2 cache.

That's 2x faster at a 10% faster CPU clock, and 1/2 the data bus rate.

Sounds like the 604 is a "hands down" winner to me...

