>   nstn1038@fox.nstn.ca (Ian R. Yokota) writes:
>  I have a DECpc XL 466d2 which has an on board NCR SCSI controller and
>  I was wondering when connecting an external SCSI device do I have to
>  remove any internal terminating resistors?
>  

Enabling the external SCSI connector via SETUP is all that is necessary to
use the external scsi port.  You should use as short a cable as possible, 
I was unable to get a 4 foot cable to work, only an 18" cable worked well
for me.

If you want truly fast scsi, consider purchasing an Adaptec AHA-2940 PCI
controller for this machine.  It is orders of magnitude better than the 
onboard NCR (I-want-to-be-a-REAL-SCSI-controller-when-I-grow-up) scsi 
controller, and it will send the spinup commands to those rz5x disks you
may have around, and is generaly the defacto standard for scsi controllers,
especially if you hook up a backup tape, everyone tests with Adaptec.

