Subject: Re: Memory Bandwidth for AlphaStations?
Date: 1995/04/19
Message-ID: <3n2vua$8th@peavax.eng.pko.dec.com>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 101268550
distribution: world
references: <3m9ivp$5af@agate.berkeley.edu> <D6up1r.MnG@world.std.com> <3mtv40$2i1@nntpd.lkg.dec.com>
organization: Digital Equipment Corporation
newsgroups: comp.sys.dec


    Bandwidth numbers for the AlphaStation 200 and 400 are as follows:


    Memory bus peak rate = 8 Bytes every 60 ns = 132 MByte/s
    Memory bus sustained throughput = 70 MByte/s (measured with McCalpin)

    PCI bus peak rate = 4 Bytes every 30 ns = 132 MByte/s
      (sustained is much lower, device dependent)

    Backup Cache peak rate = 16 Bytes every 30 ns = 528 MByte/s

    Primary Data Cache peak rate = 8 Bytes every cycle
      @233 MHz:  8 Bytes every 4.27 ns = 1866 MByte/s
      @166 MHz:  8 Bytes every 6.0 ns  = 1333 MByte/s
      @100 MHz:  8 bytes every 10.0 ns =  800 MByte/s


    Memory throughput for the AlphaStation 250 is higher due to its wider
    memory path.

