>- Have this computers SMP architecture and cache coherence ?

  Yes.

>- May system bus of 8400 support split transactions as in SGI PC
>  PowerPath2 ?

  There are several transactions in flight on the system bus
  if that's what you mean. It may not be the exact same scheme
  as that used by SGI.

>- Are data and address busses of TurboLaser different parts of 
>  system bus (i.e. are there 2 busses really) ?

  Yes. 256 bit of data path and 40 bits of address/command bus.

>- Are PCI busses connected directly to system bus or it exist
>  some intermediate intelligent equipment such as PowerChannel in
>  SGI PC ?

  The system can have multiple I/O processors which in turn have
  4 things called "hoses".  Each hose can connect to a 12 slot
  PCI bus (or XMI or Futurebus or EISA).  So it's a hierarchy.

>- Are there some estimations of prices ?

   The 8200 starts at $100,000, the 8400 around $200,000.

>- How many KW must have power source and which cooling equipment is
>  necessary for 8200/8400 systems ?

   The 8200 runs off normal single-phase power, the 8400 can need
   three-phase power in the high-end configurations (30 A US, 16 A Europe).

