While I can't comment on the speed of Alphas one thing to watch out for with
VC++ 2.0 is precompiled headers. MicroSoft does these in a funny way such that
if your code it not setup correctly they can seriously slow your compilations
down.

My advice would be to first read the documentation on precompile headers very 
carefully and then compile in verbose mode to ensure that it is not recreating 
the recompiled header for every file.

Robin

