newsgroups: comp.sys.dec


In article <3n1sa5$dp1@newsbf02.news.aol.com>, davegolden@aol.com
(DaveGolden) writes:
>I am attempting to determine if there is any latent support for the
>ISA
>version of the ATI Mach 64 board under OSF/1.  I know that the PCI
>version is supported, and perusing the kernel files leads me to
>believe
>that the ISA version should work.
>
>I'm hoping that a knowledgable DEC person will take pity on me and
>throw
>me a bone by telling me the one thing that I forgot to do (perhaps an
>"isacfg" command in console mode???).
>

  The only "supported" ATI card is the 2mb Mach64 CX (DRAM) card.  The
  code was written to handle the VRAM (GX) cards, and the ISA cards,
  but was not completely tested.  In particular, the VRAM newer VRAM
  cards use a memory type that does not support block write mode, and
  the code tries to use it, and leaves "ghost" images on some fill
  operations.

  The problems have been reported to the OSF engineers, and have been
  fixed in the VMS code for the upcomming release.

