In article <art.23.000EFC36@pmail.kmsys.com>, art@pmail.kmsys.com
(Arturo P. Jimenez, Jr.) writes:

:I'm looking for a specification on VT100, VT220 & VT320 emulation.  Does 
:anyone know where I can obtain said information?  Does DEC publish such a 
:specification?

  I'm not aware of a Digital-published specification for the emulation
  of the VT-series terminals.

  One can, however, readily acquire the programming manuals for the
  various VT-series devices -- the programming manuals include the escape
  and control sequences used by the terminals.  The core features of the
  later VT-serues terminals are typically supersets of the earlier ones.

  EK-VT3XX-TP is the Programmer Reference Manual (it's volume one of the
  reference manual and covers text programming) for the VT330/VT340 series.

  If you're just looking for the sequences themselves and have access to
  OpenVMS, ULTRIX or UNIX, you can look in Sys$System:SMGTERMS.TXT and/or
  in /etc/termcap.
  
  [If you're thinking of writing an emulator, it's probably cheaper to buy
  one.]

