The problem is that you subtracted rather than dividing!  To take an example
from the first part of the post, ".. the 5/300 (Alpha 21164/300) CPU ... is
approximately:  51 times faster than a Pentium 90".  This was apparently 
arrived at by subtracting 10 from 61.  The correct way to calculate this
example:

If x is the number of times faster that Alpha model is than the A4000 and
solving for y which is the number of times faster the Alpha is over the
P90, then

		10xy = 61x
		   y = 61x/10x
		   y = 6.1

making the Alpha 6.1 times faster than the Pentium.  Same method for the
others.
