: There are a bunch of DEC RZ disks that don't spin up on power up, and 
: don't have jumpers to set the power-on state.  These are RZ22, RZ23,
: RZ24 and RZ55/56 and I think RX57.  In order to set them to spin up on
: power up, you need some software to do it.  

: The easiest way is to use a DECstation to set the power up state, I
: think it's documented in the console commands.  A VAXstation can be
: used also, but it's a little more complicated and you have to pretend
: that the disk is a tape and set some bits.  (Kenny house, where's that
: note  you posted long ago on how to do this?)   

: Finally, if you can find someone with a Macintosh and Silverlining,
: that has the capability to set the spinup bits on SCSI disks.  Once
: set, it'll power up spin up forever.


: -bill

Final option is to call the DEC BBS 508-496-8800 and download the 
RZSPINUP.ZIP utility.  It will only run on DOS machines.  It only needs 
to be run once.
