The comment about peripherals and memory is not true.  The AlphaStations use
standard PC-style SIMMs (this is true of the AlphaStation 200 and 400 series,
I'm not sure about the 250) and the peripheral bus is industry-standard PCI.
If you choose to buy these components from sources other than Digital, the
prices will be pretty much the same as the other systems (Digital does charge
a bit more.)  Doesn't Sun use a proprietary peripheral bus in its workstations?

I'm a bit puzzled as to just what system you found in the magazine - I'm not
sure we ever made a 190MHz Alpha workstation.
