In article <3n030r$gk5@jac.zko.dec.com>,
John L. Henning <henning@i4get.enet.dec.com> wrote:
>
>        AlphaStation 250 4/266    (21064A)
>
>but this is a differently designed system with at least a unique
>motherboard, perhaps more differences as well.  If you want 266Mhz, I
>wouldn't count on being able to upgrade any of the first three models to
>this one.

One difference is that this machine has a 2Mb cache, as opposed to the
512k cache on the Alphstation 200 4/{100,166,233}.  I think it also
may have better memory bandwidth & more PCI slots, but this is all
from memory.

So, even if it were possible for the original poster to upgrade his
200 4/100 to a 200 4/266, it would still not be as fast as the 250
4/266 because of its smaller cache & possibly reduced memory bandwidth.

