Leonardo Lagos (Leonardo Lagos Mu^1^57^oz) (llagos@entel.cl) wrote:
: Hi... I want to know how can i print .ps files from an Ultrix system, to
: a DECLaser 1100 printer, but... here comes the problem... this printer
: IS NOT Postscript...!

: The DecLaser 1100 is not longer supported, and the Postscript cartridge
: is no longer available (that what's Digital says down here in Chile...!)

: I know i can install GhostScript, GhostView, and others, but the answers
: is.. if i have a .ps file... can i print it in this printer, without the
: PS cartridge?

: What can i do, if not? Maybe transform the .ps to another format?
: Is it possible to transform the .ps to .dvi and install drivers from the
: TeX distribution that can print with similar quality in the DecLaser?

Sounds strange, why go the way via TeX if you already have a PS inter-
preter (ghostscript) handy ? What is the input format of a DL 1100 ?
Is it sixel ? Then use the ln03 device. Is it PCL ? GS has drivers for
this, too. You may even enclose the correct call to gs in a script that
is installed as a printer filter, so you can transparently print PS or
ASCII.

All you _really_ need are the original Adobe Type 1 fonts. Have a look
at /usr/lib/DPS/outline/decwin (or so), they are there ;)

