>Andrew Gallatin <gallatin@hpdemo.isds.duke.edu> wrote:
>
>}We're about to order a few AlphaStation 200 4/100 boxes.  We've already
>}got a number of machines that use the RZ26L disks & find the noise to
>}be nearly unbearable.
> 
>    There is a special mounting bracket we got from DEC which
>    really quiets the the 26l's down (sorry, I don't have a
>    part#).

    There's a newer, quieter version of the RZ26L that has been shipping
    since the end of August 1994.  The old (noisy) version is A01;  the new
    (quieter) drive is B01.  There are apparently at least two versions of
    the B01 revision of the RZ26L drive.  Those marked "E06" on the side
    are alleged to be quieter than those marked "E05".  The E06 drives are
    supposed to have been shipping since November 1994 (or so).  I haven't
    heard these, so I can't comment on their relative effectiveness at
    reducing drive noise.

    The noise reduction bracket mentioned earlier in this string (part
    number 70-31748-01) will only fit in the top drive bay of the
    ALphaStation 200, because it increases the height of the drive by 0.5
    inches.  [The lower drive bay will only accomodate a one-inch-high
    drive.]  The bracket has subjectively been shown to quiet the drive
    down somewhat.  This is neither qualified nor supported, except for use
    in the DEC 3000 model 300 series workstations.

    -- Kenny 

