On 13 Apr 1995, Leonardo Lagos wrote:

> Hi... I want to know how can i print .ps files from an Ultrix system, to
> a DECLaser 1100 printer, but... here comes the problem... this printer
> IS NOT Postscript...!
Then you're pretty much screwed.  If you print it you'll get one of two 
results:
1) a set of banner pages with nothing in between, or
2) reams of ASCII garbage.

Postscript is an ASCII-based language, since ASCII is a little more 
network-friendly, etc (also explains why ps files are so damned big :)  )

If your printer doesn't know how to talk Postscript you'll need that PS 
cartridge or a new printer that has Postscript built-in.

JMS



