In article <3mh8ao$4no@news.ccit.arizona.edu>,
Jae H Shin <jshin@aruba.ccit.arizona.edu> wrote:
>subject says it all.
>i need pinouts for both color and mono.

I made this file by applying a continuity tester to the cables
that I have. Corrections on pin numbering (I made up a system for MMJ 
and mouse DIN) or anything else are welcome...

this is for vaxstation 2000s and 3100, 
and decstation 2100 and 3100.

db15 on dec stations

  Shell  --                   -- ground
  pin 1  --  ? red   bnc core                           } rgb  version
      2  --                   -- ground
      3  --  A mono  bnc shell                          } mono version
      4  --  V                ------------ mouse pin 1
      5  --  V                ------------ mouse pin 5
      6  --  V keyboard pin 2 -- ground
      7  --                   -- ground
      8  --  V keyboard pin 3 ------------ mouse pin 2
      9  --  A mono  bnc core                           } mono version
     10  --  ? green bnc core                           } rgb  version
     11  --  ? blue  bnc core                           } rgb  version
     13  --  V                ------------ mouse pin 7
     14  --  V keyboard pin 4
     15  --  V keyboard pin 1
     XX                       -- ground--- mouse pin 6

A = will work on vaxstations and decstations
V = will work on vaxstations only
? = will probably work on both vaxstations and decstations

keyboard pins are numbered as follows:
 looking at plug from front (pin) side with the MMJ tab facing up,
 and the cable leading away from you,

   ___T__
   |1234|
   ------
 ie, rightmost pin == 1, leftmost  pin == 4, MMJ tab (T) up

mouse pins are numbered as follows:
 with central indent (i) down,
 pin 1 == lower lefthand, proceed counter clockwise

      6    5
    i       i
     7  =  4
      1 2 3
        i

note that the mono monitor cables for vaxstation 3100s and decstation 2100s
are identical, but: the vaxstation 3100 will accept the keyboard
and mouse signals thru the db15 umbilical port while the decstation
2100 will not. Thus while a vax mono umbilical cable (and, I suspect,
color umbilical cable) could be used as a monitor cable for a
decstation, the keyboard and mouse must still be plugged into their
respective ports on the back of the CPU case rather than into the umbilical.




