Nik Tumbri (nicolast@ariel.unimelb.edu.au) wrote:
: Howd'y...

: I'm interested in upgrading one of my QBUS 11's to a uVAX II, to eventually
: run NetBSD. (<- This is going to happen, yes?)  I have stacks of QBus backpanes
: and cards (Disk controlers, Serial Ports, Ethernet and a few other odds and
: sods), so I assume all I need is a uVAX II board + a matching memory board,
: yes?

So long as you have a Q22 backplane with C/D interconnect for the first few
slots, that is basically correct. (You will also need a couple of cables
and either a MicroVAXII back panel insert or the pinouts of the two console
connectors on the KA630 to help make your own. I can give you the pinouts
if you need them, although it would be a lot easier if you can find an
insert.)

As for NetBSD, it is currently up multiuser on a MicroVAXII, but would
still be considered pre-Alpha. At this time there is no binary distribution
(no-one has succeeded in building a complete user land from NetBSD sources
yet:-), but hopefully in the next few months..

If you are interested in the port, you should subscribe to the mailing
list by sending the following msg. to majordomo@netbsd.org.

subscribe port-vax <your email address>

Good luck with it, rick





