X-Deja-AN: 100178970
organization: Center for Image Analysis, Uppsala, Sweden
newsgroups: comp.sys.dec

I use this script to backup a disk on a OSF system to a tape drive
on a ULTRIX system. The script is started on the ULTRIX machine and
runs rdump via rsh on the OSF machine.


#!/bin/csh
rsh bamse -l root /usr/sbin/rdump 0uf puh:/dev/nrmt0h /usr/home3 >>&! /var/spool/mqueue/home-3
mt -f /dev/rmt0h rewoff
 
The backup media is a TLZ04 DAT tape where about 1.2 GB can be stored. The
strange thing is that a @GB rz28 can be "stored" on one tape.

Even more strange is that the script successfully runs even if no tape is
loaded in the DAT-station, rdump reports everythins as normal. Clearly there
are some communication problem between rmt and rdump



