X-Deja-AN: 100353060
references: <3lumdg$ljd@theopolis.orl.mmc.com> <3m1ogs$8a7@jac.zko.dec.com> <3mc5eg$i7s@theopolis.orl.mmc.com>
organization: The Ohio State University, Department of Computer and Information Science
newsgroups: comp.sys.dec

Well, for what it's worth, I have a DEClaser 2150 attached to my PC. I run
WFW 3.11.  I NEVER use the printer in PostScript mode unless I'm printing
PostScript files that I've pulled off the wire.  I find that the DEC ANSI
driver (on my machine, I use the DEClaser 2100+ driver) will produce print
anywhere from 2-10 times as fast as the 2150 PostScript driver, running from
the same PC with the same file from the same application, particularly
if there are any graphics embedded in the files.  The 2100+ driver, using
TrueType fonts, can actually keep the printer running at several pages per
minute for the average MS Word document.

I don't know if the driver produces inefficient PostScript, or if the
PS implementation is slow in these printers, but that's been my experience.

Eric Osborne




