From: srlnrow@alpha.gns.cri.nz
Subject: Summary: Fonts in Solaris xterm on DECWindows
Date: 1995/04/10
Message-ID: <3maa10$n2h@st-james.comp.vuw.ac.nz>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 100261759
organization: Institute of Geological & Nuclear Sciences
newsgroups: comp.sys.dec,comp.os.vms

In answer to my query on how to get a Sun xterm to respond to its menu font
choices (ie, Ctrl/mouse button) on DECWindows, Tom Gaps of Merix
Corporation pointed me towards defining some XTerm*fontn resources to
suitable choices in the DECW$XDEFAULTS.DAT file. These other choices are
needed, because the default XTerm resources on Solaris use aliases (eg
names like 7x14) that are by default unknown to the DECWindows server.
Alternatively the XTerm aliases can be defined as documented in the file
installed on my system as SYS$HELP:DECW$TROUBLESHOOTING_GUIDE.TXT, viz

   For fixed-width fonts, such as 6x10, copy the file
   DECW$EXAMPLES:DECW$FONT_ALIAS_ FILENAMES.DAT to the
   SYS$COMMON:[SYSFONT.DECW.USER_COMMON] directory. You must end the
   current session and start a new session for the change to take effect.

I did this and the XTerm font menus now work.
-- 
Roger Williams, Institute of Geological & Nuclear Sciences, New Zealand
