A topic that has been on this newsgroup many a time is the problem
of the INDEX FILE FULL and/or HEADER FULL.

A product that will fix this problem wil be announced at the DECUS in
Washington DC, May 8-10. Come over to PSS, Inc at Booth 334 and have
a chat with the developer Keith Walls on how he did it. The name of the
product is OpenToolBox: DiskMaster. (tm) This is the second product in the
OpenToolBox product family, the first one is 1995 Target Award Nominee
MemoryMaster.

The main reason for this new product is to *prevent disk downtime*. As
you know disk downtime costs many times the initial purchase price per
megabyte.

OpenToolBox: DiskMaster can also defragment INDEXF.SYS when you
specify the  /defrag qualifier. DiskMaster runs in two modes: online and
offline.  In 95% of the cases the problem can be fixed online and your users
won't even notice. In 5%  you will need to address the problem offline but
better said near-line.

Here is some example output:

An online where nothing is necessary:

$ dm
DiskMaster> rep dva0
%DSKMASTER-S-NOREPIBMAP, volume has 2754 unused headers; not changed
%DSKMASTER-S-NOREPINDEX, index file has space to be extended at least
36 times; not changed
%DSKMASTER-S-NOREPAIRNEC, volume does not need repair

And an offline where nothing needs to be done:

DiskMaster> rep/off dva0/def
%MOUNT-I-MOUNTED, FRED mounted on _DYSON$DVA0:
%DSKMASTER-I-INDEXFCTG, INDEXF.SYS is as contiguous as ODS-2 will allow
DiskMaster>

An online where there was something to do:

$ crea dka200:[0,0]x.x
%CREATE-E-OPENOUT, error opening DKA200:[0,0]X.X; as output
-RMS-E-CRE, ACP file create failed
-SYSTEM-W-IDXFILEFULL, index file is full
$ dm repair dka200
%DSKMASTER-S-NOREPINDEX, index file has space to be extended at least
22 times; not changed
%DSKMASTER-I-MAPEXTEND, index file bit map is to be extended to allow
2086 more headers
%DSKMASTER-S-IBMEXTEND, index file bitmap extended to allow for 2086
extra file headers
$ crea dka200:[0,0]x.x
a new file
^Z
$


And an offline where there is something to do (forced by /defrag):

$ dm
DiskMaster> rep/off/defr dka200
%MOUNT-I-MOUNTED, FRED mounted on _DYSON$DKA200:
%DSKMASTER-I-DEFRAGIF, attempting to defragment INDEXF.SYS
%DSKMASTER-I-DEFRAGGED, INDEXF.SYS fragmentation reduced from 33 to 5
extents
DiskMaster> ^Z


We go into field test April 17-th and expect to ship May 15, after the DECUS.

Warm regards,
Stu Sjouwerman.

