>I am trying to set up my comms software to emulate a VT320 terminal and
>need to know what characters or character sequences get transmitted to
>the host computer by the function keys and editing keys on a VT320
>terminal. Can anyone help?

This kind of stuff shows up on comp.terminals all the time. But...

The general format is:

<ESC>[Pn~, where Pn is:

Editing keypad: left-to-right, top-to-bottom, 1 through 6
Top row: left-to-right, starting with F6, 17 through 34, but, you have to 
count the spaces between the blocks of function keys--the space between F10 
and F11 would be 22, for instance, which can't be sent by any key.
