You could be flirting with disaster if you don't check up on your
configuration.   When the DEC 3000 series was announced (the 3000/400
was one of the first machines) DEC specifically said that the RZ57 was
not a supported device. 

Although the RZ57 was not sold when the Alpha systems came out, many
people were upgrading prior generation VAXstation and DECstation
systems with RZ57 and Digital went through severe pain to try and make
sure that no RZ57 disks were attached to Alpha systems.  

When I left Digital, there was an effort ongoing to see if an
engineering fix could be put in place to remove the restriction, and
some solutions had been proposed, but I left before anything came out. 

I'd go back to the person you bought the system from and complain.  DEC
sales and marketing went to great pains to try to ensure that people
didn't connect RZ57's to these systems and had never listed the device
as "supported" in the SPD (Software Product Description) for VMS or
OSF/1.    


Bill Jackson




