Hi Andre,

The product you need to review is called EDA/SQL from Information Builders. 
EDA/SQL is a host based product that will take the targeted platform and turn 
it into a client/server system.

All in all, this is a superior product with unparalled functionality and is an 
open environment. EDA/SQL is avalible for over 15 differ platforms and OS's. 
The lastest innovation from IBI is data location transparency meaning that you 
can connect to a single host and it will maintain the catalogs for the data 
locations so that the user or developer does not have to worry about the 
originator or destination. The product provides interfaces to over 65 
differnent databases and file types.

The magic for developers on different platforms is a single consistent API. 
The API calls are identical on all platforms and there are only about 30 API 
calls total. You only need to use about 7 or 8 of them to create a robust c/s 
application. As for a single user interface, you could use any one of the 
platforms or create an application on the PC using about any tool you want 
ranging from VB, PB, C, C++, Smalltalk, etc. etc...

All the user or developer has to do to get the data is issue a SQL request and 
EDA/SQL will handle the rest even if the data isn't in a relational format. As 
an added benefit, EDA/SQL will also provide heterogeneous joins across 
platforms!


If you need any more info, email me at ericc@airmail.net

Good luck...

