:Toshiba America Electronic Components
:bill_jackson@taec.e-mail.com

    I'm not sure what the goal is here -- the base noter *has* X Windows.

    The VAXstation 3100 was generally sold with DECwindows -- which is X
    Windows, and it has the X Windows libraries.  More recent workstations
    are sold with DECwindows Motif -- DECwindows Motif is (still) available
    for the VAXstation 3100.  And if you are presently using DECterms, you
    *have* X Windows (DECwindows).  You can upgrade (for a price) to more
    recent OpenVMS and DECwindows Motif versions -- if you would like.

    More recent versions of DECwindows and DECwindows Motif can both use
    DECnet, local and (if one is available) TCP/IP transports.  (I'm not
    certain when the DECwindows TCP/IP transport support first shipped
    for use with third-party TCP/IP packages such as TWG.)

	--

    The package that converts the VAXstation 3100 into an X Terminal is
    EWS: QL-YWRA*-**, QL-YWRAC-RA is for the VAXstation 3100 "target".
    EWS is normally set up to be downloaded into the target workstation,
    which means you'll need another system (and an associated license
    and binary kit) on which the EWS download can be performed.

