Eddie -

> 
I am trying to set up my comms software to emulate a VT320 terminal and
> need to know what characters or character sequences get transmitted to
> the host computer by the function keys and editing keys on a VT320
> terminal. Can anyone help?

    You can find this information in the programming guide for almost
and DEC CRT of vintage VT220 or later. In brief, the keys are:

    Find        <CSI>1~
    Insert Here <CSI>2~
    Remove      <CSI>3~
    Select      <CSI>4~
    Prev Screen <CSI>5~
    Next Screen <CSI>6~
    PF1         <SS3>P
    PF2         <SS3>Q
    PF3         <SS3>R
    PF4         <SS3>S
    F6          <CSI>17~
    F7          <CSI>18~
    F8          <CSI>19~
    F9          <CSI>20~
    F10         <CSI>21~
    F11         <CSI>23~ (yes, they skip a number)
    F12         <CSI>24~
    F13         <CSI>25~
    F14         <CSI>26~
    Help        <CSI>28~ (skipped another one)
    Do          <CSI>29~
    F17         <CSI>31~ (and another)
    F18         <CSI>32~
    F19         <CSI>33~
    F20         <CSI>34~

