Hello folks.

Recently I acquired a disk drive for use at my DECstation 2100.
Unfortunately it isn't an original DEC RX23 drive but a TEAC FC-1
(originating from a HP 710 afaik).
Perhaps anybody can tell me what I'm missing in using it ?  See below.

Ok, so I took the parcel from the post office and connected the drive
to the machine.  Minor hassle number one: the screws together with
the placeholders that I bough to fasten the Fujitsu hard disk to the
inner chassis board will settle the drive way into the box so I will
have to buy different placeholders sooner or later...

Turn machine on, issue "test -c" in console monitor - everything fine.
So I booted the machine and tried to access a floppy disk.  I have
copies of working mtools but 'mdir' gave me some kind of "MEDIA ERROR".
'rzdisk -i' gives me the same and the drive's data just fine.
After lots of thinking I edited /sys/data/scsi_data.c so that the entry
for the RX23 is matched with the drive's ID-string.  I remade the
kernel and booted.  Now the system identifies the drive as a RX23.
The "MEDIA ERROR" is gone, but 'mdir' doesn't give the contents of a
properly formatted disk.  'dd' doesn't read anything either.
Next try: blank disk and 'rzdisk -f' to format it.  Gives me a wierd
error message with "illegal request" or somesuch.

Now I connected the drive to my humble Atari ST to see what that does
with it.  I run 'icdformat' and formatting the disk works just fine.
Now this software takes the disk for some kind of winchester media
such as a Syquest drive and lets me partition it.  I do wonder though
that it reports about 5000 blocks which would relate to a ED disk...
The current situation is that the disk isn't accepted at boot time on
the Atari ST (thus no driveletter is assigned for filesystem level
access), but I can use a disk monitor to read the root sector of the
disk just fine.  I think my ICDBOOT driver (v 5.xx) doesn't know
about removable media etc, so I might have to hunt for a v 6.xx, but
otherwise the drive seems to work good on the Atari ST.


Now, has anyone ever used a floppy disk drive on a DECstation that isn't
a RX23 or RX26 ?  What is the interface between the drive and the
machine besides it being addressed like any other SCSI unit ?  We have
a machine at the university with an original RX23 connected to it (that's
where I took the binary copy of the mtools, but I do have the sources
available as well) and it is addressed as /dev/rz1c.

Greetings,
