+ I want check my RZ25L after installation into DEC 3000/300LX. I have
+ important data on this disk. I want  run
+ >>>test scsi verify . But in example in Hardware Reference Guide
+ on p.4-64 I look that there is DKA500 OK ? question at running of this
+ test. But if I'm correct , this request may arrive only in the cases
+ of danger of data destroyes. May somebody inform be, does verify
+ test really destroy some data on disk ?
  
The documentation doesn't give any warning about this test being a destructive
test.  It just says that if verifies that all blocks on the disk can be read.

If this a UNIX (formerly OSF/1) system you're talking about, then there's 
another way to do a read-only test.  Use a utility called scu(8).   eg:

	# scu -f /dev/rrz5c
	scu>  verify media starting 0

Note:  Use "verify", not "scan".  Scan does a write/read destructive test.

-- 
