> I want to run >>> TEST SCSI VERIFY.
> Does verify test really destroy some data on disk ?

        Disk Verifier Utility

        This utility will verify that all blocks on the disk can be read.

        Steps to be taken are as follows:

        o Issue INQUIRY command to make sure the device is a disk
        o Issue a START UNIT command to spin up a hard disk
        o Issue a READ CAPACITY command to obtain device capacity
        o Issue VERIFY command

 All of these SCSI commands are non-destructive.

