In article <33fekj$ibh@uuneo.neosoft.com>, jleslie@dmccorp.com 
(Jerry Leslie) writes:
|> Pardon a newbie question, but I haven't seen any non-DEC systems 
|> referred to in this news group.
|> 
|> Are there any other vendors, besides DEC, offering now, or planning to
|> offer OSF/1 ?

OSF produces generic releases that different companies customize for their
own environments.  DEC decided to call their port of OSF's OSF/1 to the
alpha platform OSF/1.  I know of other companies that have done the same, but
they call their OS's by different names.  (I'm not sure if I am allowed to
name names here.)

There are other companies who have used our commands and libraries (XPG4)
with their own kernel.  Some companies may want to use just our 
Internationalization code.

BTW OSF's OSF/1 release numbers have nothing to do with DEC's OSF/1 release 
number. We (OSF) have just released our OSF/1 R1.3 which is a micro kernel 
based OS.

This news group really discusses DEC's OSF/1, not OSF's OSF/1.

