Space Center Division of McDonnell Douglas Space and Defense Systems 
(MDS&DS-KSC).  Our offices are at the Kennedy Space Center, which is 
located on the east coast of central Florida.

The Database Administrators will support planning and coordinating the
creation of computerized databases including base definition, structure, 
documentation, long-range requirements, operational guidelines and security.
Responsibilities include ensuring the accuracy and completeness of data in
files, tables and various support tools.  Also required are database design and
integration of complex systems, providing appropriate consulting, interfacing,
and training for other data processing sections, users and management.  The
Administrators will help formulate policies, procedures and standards relating
to database management and monitor transaction activity and utilization.
Preparation and analysis of activity, progress and performance reports is 
expected.  The Administrators will establish and maintain database level
security and integrity controls to ensure the protection of data against
unauthorized disclosure, accidental or intentional loss of data, or
unauthorized modification..

We are looking for individuals with a four year degree in computer 
science and a minimum of six years of work-related experience who are
familiar with applications development, relational data base technologies 
and have had Database Administration experience with Oracle's
RDB, SQL, C, and Digital's VMS Operating System.

