	Essentially, you can't.  The VXT images on the InfoServer and those
that load "host based" are different. The InfoServer images use the InfoServer
for font service, configuration and demand paging.

	The host based images run in memory on the VXT and require at least a
10 meg VXT.  The font services can come from any of several sources, but are
usually from the boot host.  You will need to get the VXT software for UNIX
hosts. (That may not be the exact name.)

	I'm an InfoServer Engineer, not a VXT engineer but I do understand some
of the basic differences between the host-based and InfoServer based images.


