Hi Craig !

Let me tell you about pdcmd properties for the moment.
We figured out that:

1) Everything works fine if temperature is below 20 C .
   According to its specification it should work at
   range  10 C to 40 C ( 50 F to 104 F ).

2) In case of T > 20 C :
   a) Everything works fine if we do nothing with 
      tape drives.
   b) After we start to work with tape drive(s) things
      are going fine about 5 - 30 minutes. After that
      we get the console message:

      SCSI bus 0: resetting bus

      At that time we see that all drives are rewinding
      tapes. The computer itself is not rebooted mostly.
      Disks continue work at this time.
      But sometimes ( looks like swap i/o happens at
      the same time ) the computer goes down.

      After that one of the tape drives becomes "bad".
      Any first i/o request to that drive forces 
      SCSI reset. And only reboot ( we tried to switch
      on/off drive power , down temperature ) can return the
      "bad" drive to the "good" status.

  Could you ask decstation guru about this problem ?

   Best regards . 
       Andrey.




